  "lineage": "The fast triple-metre dance-song of Aragón in north-east Spain, crystallised in the nineteenth century around Zaragoza and Calatayud and institutionalised through the certamen oficial de jota from 1912 — brisk 3/8 or 3/4 at roughly 130-160 beats per minute, a rondalla of bandurrias, laúdes and guitars strumming a hard I-V-I ostinato, castanets on the dance, and coplas of four octosyllabic lines sung at extreme volume in a high open chest register with long held cadential notes.",
